---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro'

const bugReport = 'https://github.com/PaulWoitaschek/Voice/issues/new?template=bug.yml'
---

<Prose
  description="Find out why an audiobook doesn't play right in Voice, and fix it in your browser."
  title="Check an audiobook file"
>
  <h1>Does your book play right?</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    If a book doesn't show up in Voice, doesn't start, stops early or jumps to the wrong place, the cause is often the
    file. Check it here. Your file doesn't leave your device.
  </p>

  <div class="tool" data-state="idle">
    <label class="button primary pick">
      Choose an audiobook file
      <input type="file" />
    </label>
    <div class="checking">
      <p class="file"></p>
      <progress aria-label="Checking" class="check-progress" max="1"></progress>
    </div>
    <div class="result">
      <p class="file"></p>
      <p data-verdict="unreadable">
        This page can't read the file. It may be damaged, locked with DRM like Audible's AAX files, or in a format Voice
        doesn't play, like WMA. See the <a href="#fix">ways to fix it</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="problem">
        <span data-verdict="format">Voice can't play the audio in this file. It's <span class="format"></span>.</span>
        <span data-verdict="seek">
          In this file, a jump can land up to <span class="amount"></span> away from where it should.
        </span>{' '}
        <span class="here">Convert it to M4B to fix this, here or in one of the <a href="#fix">other ways</a>.</span>
        <span class="elsewhere">Convert it to M4B to fix this. See the <a href="#fix">ways to fix it</a>.</span>
      </p>
      <p data-verdict="fine">
        No known problem found. If Voice still doesn't play it right, please <a href={bugReport}>report a bug</a> and
        paste the details below.
      </p>
      <label class="details-label" for="details">Details for a bug report</label>
      <textarea id="details" readonly></textarea>
      <div class="actions">
        <button class="button tonal small copy" type="button">Copy</button>
        <button class="button primary small convert" type="button">Convert to M4B</button>
        <button class="button tonal small again" type="button">Check another file</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="working">
      <p class="file"></p>
      <progress aria-label="Converting" class="convert-progress" max="1"></progress>
      <p class="muted status"></p>
      <button class="button tonal small cancel" type="button">Cancel</button>
    </div>
    <div class="done">
      <p class="file"></p>
      <p class="muted status"></p>
      <a class="button primary download">Download</a>
      <button class="button tonal small again" type="button">Check another file</button>
    </div>
    <p class="error" role="alert"></p>
    <p aria-live="polite" class="announce"></p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="why">Why MP3 books jump</h2>
  <p>
    Most audiobook MP3 files change their bitrate as they go. To find a time in such a file, a player has only a rough
    map with 100 points. In a book of 10 hours, that map can be off by minutes. M4B files have an exact map, so Voice can
    always go to the right place.
  </p>

  <h2 id="other-players">Why other players seem fine</h2>
  <p>
    Most players use the same rough map. In a test book, VLC started a minute early when it jumped to 5:30:00. You
    notice it more in Voice, because Voice jumps more often: it goes back a few seconds each time you pause, and it
    jumps to your place each time it loads the book. A player that plays from start to end never has to find a time.
  </p>

  <h2 id="fix">Ways to fix it</h2>
  <p>
    After each of them, put the new file in your audiobook folder and remove the old file, so Voice doesn't show the book
    twice.
  </p>

  <h3>In your browser</h3>
  <p>The converter above turns the book into an M4B file.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your book doesn't leave your device. Your browser does the conversion.</li>
    <li>The title, author and cover stay in the new file. So do the chapters of an MP3 file.</li>
    <li>The audio becomes AAC at 64 kbps, which is about 29 MB per hour.</li>
    <li>
      The whole book has to fit in memory. For very long books, use a computer, and keep the tab open until the download
      starts.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>With Audiobookshelf</h3>
  <p>
    If your books are on an Audiobookshelf server, edit the book, open <strong>Tools</strong>,
    and choose <strong>Make M4B Audiobook File</strong>.
  </p>

  <h3>With ffmpeg</h3>
  <p>
    A damaged M4B file often plays again after <a href="https://ffmpeg.org/download.html">ffmpeg</a> writes it new. This
    keeps the audio and the chapters as they are:
  </p>
  <pre><code>ffmpeg -i "book.m4b" -map 0:a -map_chapters 0 -c copy "fixed.m4b"</code></pre>
  <p>To convert any other book to M4B:</p>
  <pre><code>ffmpeg -i "book.mp3" -map 0:a -map "0:v?" -c:a aac -b:a 64k -c:v copy -disposition:v attached_pic "book.m4b"</code></pre>
  <p>
    To keep the MP3 audio as it is, split the book into 10 minute files instead. Voice plays all files in a folder as
    one book, but the chapter names are lost. Make the folder <code>book</code> first:
  </p>
  <pre><code>ffmpeg -i "book.mp3" -map 0:a -c copy -f segment -segment_time 600 -reset_timestamps 1 "book/part %03d.mp3"</code></pre>

  <h3>Books with DRM</h3>
  <p>
    A book from a store that locks it with DRM, like Audible, only plays in the store's app. Voice can't play it, and
    this page can't convert it.
  </p>
</Prose>

<script>
  import { checkFile, plural } from '../scripts/check'

  const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.tool')!
  const input = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('input')!
  const checkProgress = root.querySelector<HTMLProgressElement>('.check-progress')!
  const convertProgress = root.querySelector<HTMLProgressElement>('.convert-progress')!
  const details = root.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>('#details')!
  const copy = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.copy')!
  const download = root.querySelector<HTMLAnchorElement>('.download')!
  const error = root.querySelector('.error')!
  const announce = root.querySelector('.announce')!
  const focusFor: Record<string, HTMLElement | null> = {
    idle: input,
    result: copy,
    working: root.querySelector('.cancel'),
    done: download,
  }
  let file: File | undefined
  let cancel: (() => Promise<void>) | undefined
  let conversionId = 0

  const show = (state: string, status = '') => {
    const changed = root.dataset.state !== state
    root.dataset.state = state
    root.querySelectorAll(`.${state} .status`).forEach((element) => (element.textContent = status))
    if (changed) focusFor[state]?.focus()
  }

  const showResult = () => {
    show('result')
    const verdict = [...root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.result p:not(.file)')].find((p) => p.checkVisibility())
    announce.textContent = verdict?.innerText ?? ''
  }

  input.addEventListener('change', async () => {
    file = input.files?.[0]
    if (!file) return
    input.value = ''
    root.querySelectorAll('.file').forEach((element) => (element.textContent = file!.name))
    error.textContent = ''
    announce.textContent = ''
    checkProgress.removeAttribute('value')
    show('checking')
    const check = await checkFile(file, (value) => (checkProgress.value = value))
    root.querySelector('.format')!.textContent = check.format ?? ''
    root.querySelector('.amount')!.textContent = check.amount ?? ''
    details.value = check.details
    details.rows = check.details.split('\n').length
    root.dataset.verdict = check.verdict
    root.dataset.convert = String(check.canConvert)
    showResult()
  })

  copy.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    await navigator.clipboard.writeText(details.value)
    copy.textContent = 'Copied'
    setTimeout(() => (copy.textContent = 'Copy'), 2000)
  })

  root.querySelector('.convert')!.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    if (!file) return
    const name = file.name
    const id = ++conversionId
    error.textContent = ''
    announce.textContent = ''
    convertProgress.removeAttribute('value')
    show('working', 'Starting…')
    const started = performance.now()
    try {
      const { startConversion } = await import('../scripts/convert')
      const { conversion, result } = await startConversion(file, (value) => {
        if (id !== conversionId) return
        convertProgress.value = value
        const left = value > 0.01 ? ((performance.now() - started) / value) * (1 - value) : NaN
        show('working', `${Math.floor(value * 100)} %` + (isNaN(left) ? '' : ` · about ${minutes(left)} left`))
      })
      const stop = () => conversion.cancel()
      if (id === conversionId) cancel = stop
      else stop()
      const { blob, chapters } = await result
      if (id !== conversionId) return
      cancel = undefined
      URL.revokeObjectURL(download.href)
      download.href = URL.createObjectURL(blob)
      download.download = name.replace(/\.[^.]*$/, '') + '.m4b'
      show('done', `${(blob.size / 1e6).toFixed(0)} MB, ${plural(chapters, 'chapter')}`)
      announce.textContent = `Converted. ${root.querySelector('.done .status')!.textContent}`
    } catch (e) {
      if (id !== conversionId) return
      cancel = undefined
      error.textContent = "This file couldn't be converted."
      show('result')
      console.error(e)
    }
  })

  root.querySelector('.cancel')!.addEventListener('click', () => {
    conversionId++
    cancel?.()
    cancel = undefined
    showResult()
  })

  root.querySelectorAll('.again').forEach((button) =>
    button.addEventListener('click', () => {
      URL.revokeObjectURL(download.href)
      download.removeAttribute('href')
      file = undefined
      error.textContent = ''
      show('idle')
    }),
  )

  const minutes = (ms: number) => plural(Math.max(1, Math.round(ms / 60_000)), 'minute')
</script>

<style>
  .tool {
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
    justify-items: start;
    margin-block: 32px 48px;
    padding: clamp(20px, 4vw, 32px);
    border: 1px solid var(--card-line);
    border-radius: 28px;
    background: var(--card);
  }

  .tool p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .pick,
  .tool button {
    border: 0;
    font-family: inherit;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .pick input,
  .announce {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip-path: inset(50%);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .tool .download {
    color: var(--on-primary);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .pick:focus-within {
    outline: 3px solid var(--primary);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .checking,
  .result,
  .working,
  .done {
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
    justify-items: start;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .tool:not([data-state='idle']) .pick,
  .tool:not([data-state='checking']) .checking,
  .tool:not([data-state='result']) .result,
  .tool:not([data-state='working']) .working,
  .tool:not([data-state='done']) .done,
  .tool:not([data-verdict='unreadable']) [data-verdict='unreadable'],
  .tool:not([data-verdict='format']) [data-verdict='format'],
  .tool:not([data-verdict='seek']) [data-verdict='seek'],
  .tool:not([data-verdict='fine']) [data-verdict='fine'],
  .tool:not([data-verdict='format'], [data-verdict='seek']) .problem,
  .tool:not([data-convert='true']) :is(.here, .convert),
  .tool[data-convert='true'] .elsewhere {
    display: none;
  }

  .details-label {
    margin-top: 8px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  textarea {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--card-line);
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: var(--page);
    color: var(--text);
    font: 0.95rem/1.5 ui-monospace, monospace;
    resize: none;
    field-sizing: content;
  }

  .actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .file {
    font-weight: 600;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  progress {
    width: 100%;
    height: 8px;
    accent-color: var(--primary);
  }

  .error:empty {
    display: none;
  }

  .error {
    color: light-dark(#ba1a1a, #ffb4ab);
  }
</style>
